From 0b0e167c9469bbdf416e2d92ab8735e946284c9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:40:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] execute_code: bound every remote file-RPC result;
 ship lone surrogates as escapes

Follow-up to PR #2027 review 5888803485 (card t_01a1d43e5362ab4d).

1. Measure what ships. The terminal() encoded cap measured with
   encode('utf-8', 'surrogatepass') while _remote_write (and the local
   socket's sendall) encoded strict UTF-8, so a lone surrogate in a result
   (read_file decodes undecodable bytes with surrogateescape) passed the
   measurement and then raised in the sender: the poller never answered and
   the local socket thread died. One helper, _wire_bytes, now produces the
   shipped bytes for both transports and for the cap: each lone surrogate
   becomes its \uXXXX escape, which inside a JSON string decodes back to the
   same text in the sandbox.

2. Bound every remote result. Only terminal() results were capped; any other
   file-RPC result (read_file, web_extract, search_files, ...) still went
   through _remote_write at any size, embedded in a heredoc command on
   modal/daytona/vercel (Modal's legacy stdin buffer is 2 MB). A remote result
   over the same 1 MiB of shipped UTF-8 now becomes an error naming its size
   and the limit (result_bytes / limit_bytes), recorded in the call log so
   execute_code's tool_errors reports it. The local socket keeps no cap.

Tests (RED before, GREEN after): lone surrogate through the poller and the
local socket, a terminal result whose surrogatepass size fits but whose
shipped size does not stays windowed, and a 3 MB read_file result becomes the
size error. The file-RPC test helper now stops after a few polls instead of
spinning forever when a ship raises.

Real round trip (item 3): the 'Remote terminal backends' CI lane covers only
ssh + docker and may hold no secrets, so Modal cannot run there. A one-off
manual smoke on hermes-worker-3 with the broker's user/modal token
(TERMINAL_ENV=modal, worktree code): a 900 KB terminal() result
(909,190 bytes JSON) crossed the real Modal file-RPC and arrived whole,
truncated false; a 1.5 MB one came back windowed, truncated true, with its
spill path.
